{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nMigrate eligible OpenAI providers to the pydantic-ai **Responses API** as a config cutover with a\npre-v1 deprecation of the Chat-Completions fallback. The blocking research ticket\n`ageless-ferny-ugandakob` (b612-1edb-efa9-4c61, CLOSED) produced the capability matrix and the\ncontract tests (`tests/unit/test_openai_responses_contract.py`, already landed and green for both\nprefixes). Its verdict, which this ticket implements verbatim:\n\n- **Only hosted OpenAI (matrix row 1)** — bare `openai:`/inferred `gpt-*`/`o1`/`o3`/`chatgpt`,\n  with NO custom endpoint — is Responses-ready under the pinned pydantic-ai 1.107.2.\n- **Every other row is Chat-Completions-only or UNKNOWN** and stays on `openai-chat:`:\n  custom `base_url` builder (row 2), per-candidate `endpoint` override (row 3), `gateway/openai`\n  (4), `deepseek`/`grok`/`moonshotai`/`heroku`/`cerebras` (5-7), `xai`/`groq` (8, UNKNOWN),\n  vendor-side `/v1/responses` (9, UNKNOWN/moot under the pin).\n- The migration's edit-set is the **four constraint sites** the matrix named.\n\nOperator decision (2026-08-19, recorded on this ticket): **config cutover APPROVED** with a\nper-provider fallback to `openai-chat:` that is **explicitly temporary** — it carries a\ndeprecation notice and is **scheduled for removal before v1**.\n\n## Design\n\n**Default flip (the cutover).** Hosted OpenAI now resolves to `openai-responses:` by default. A\ncustom OpenAI-compatible endpoint (top-level `base_url`, per-class slot `endpoint`, or\nper-candidate `endpoint`) keeps resolving to `openai-chat:` — matrix rows 2-3: rebar's\n`_build_openai` registers only under `openai`/`openai-chat`, an `openai-responses:` string never\nreaches it, and vendor `/v1/responses` support for custom servers is UNKNOWN, so flipping a\ncustom endpoint would silently ignore its `base_url`.\n\n**The fallback IS the explicit `openai-chat:` qualifier** (or `provider = \"openai-chat\"`), now a\nDEPRECATED compatibility surface. It is per-provider/per-slot because each model-class slot,\nfallback candidate, or `cfg.model` names its own qualifier. Writing it for **hosted** OpenAI emits\na once-per-run deprecation notice pointing to `openai-responses:`, registered in the central\n`rebar._deprecations` registry as `cfg:openai-chat` with `remove_in = \"v1.0.0\"` (the repo's\nsingle-sourced pre-v1 removal horizon `_deprecations._MAJOR`). Chat forced by a **custom\nendpoint** does NOT warn (it is a construction constraint, not a deprecated opt-in, and no\nResponses alternative exists for it).\n\nPortability: this is a pure config-resolution/provider change with no CI-provider dependency; the\ndeprecation horizon is a static repo constant, and all new tests run in-process against an\n`httpx.MockTransport` stub with no network or provider credentials.\n\n## Edit-set (RED->GREEN)\n\n1. `src/rebar/llm/config.py` — add `\"openai-responses\"` to `KNOWN_PROVIDER_NAMES` so\n   `split_provider_qualifier`/`infer_provider` treat `openai-responses:` as a qualifier.\n2. `src/rebar/llm/providers.py` — add `openai-responses` to the set\n   `_pydantic_ai_known_providers()` returns (a new `_EXTRA_KNOWN_PROVIDERS` frozenset for names\n   `infer_provider` special-cases but `known_model_names()` omits), so\n   `ProviderSession.is_resolvable(\"openai-responses\")` is True and the runner leaves it a lazy\n   string for pydantic-ai to build `OpenAIResponsesModel`. The rebar builder stays chat-only.\n3. `src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py` — add `\"openai-responses\": _resolve_openai` to\n   `_PROFILE_RESOLVERS` so capability resolution no longer degrades (native_structured_output\n   parity with `openai-chat:`).\n4. `src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py` — `_resolve_target` grows an `endpoint: str | None = None`\n   param; an `_openai_family_target(tail, requested, endpoint)` helper returns `openai-chat:` for\n   an explicit `openai-chat` request or when an endpoint is present, else `openai-responses:`\n   (keeps `_resolve_target` under the C901 ceiling). Thread `endpoint` from the callers that hold\n   it: `resolve_class`/`resolve_fallback_chain` (slot/target endpoint), `primary_endpoint_for`,\n   `fallback_targets_for`, `build_fallback_model` — so the identity-matching those functions do on\n   `_resolve_target` output stays consistent with what `resolve_class` produced.\n5. `src/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py` — `_pai_model`: explicit `openai-chat:` passes through;\n   bare `openai:` resolves to `openai-chat:` when `cfg.base_url` is set, else `openai-responses:`.\n6. `src/rebar/llm/runner.py` — after `resolved` and the effective `cfg.base_url` (incl. recovered\n   slot endpoint) are known, emit the `cfg:openai-chat` notice once when `resolved` is hosted\n   `openai-chat:` (starts with `openai-chat:` AND no `base_url`).\n7. `src/rebar/_deprecations.py` — register the `cfg:openai-chat` scheduled deprecation.\n8. Docs: `docs/config-reference.md` + `docs/llm-framework.md` — document the wire-semantic change,\n   how to exercise the `openai-chat:` fallback, its deprecation and the `v1.0.0` removal target.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Update the intended behavioural-diff assertions (now `openai-responses:` for hosted openai):\n  `tests/unit/test_provider_qualifier.py` (incl. the `_KNOWN_24`->`_KNOWN_25` drift set),\n  `tests/unit/test_pydantic_ai_runner.py`, `tests/unit/test_model_classes.py`,\n  `tests/unit/test_llm_capabilities.py`.\n- New assertions: hosted `openai:`/`gpt-4o` -> `openai-responses:`; `openai:` + endpoint (top-level\n  and per-slot) stays `openai-chat:`; explicit `openai-chat:` stays chat; `is_resolvable` and\n  capabilities parity for `openai-responses:`; the deprecation notice fires once for hosted\n  `openai-chat:` and NOT for endpoint-forced chat.\n- Re-run the landed contract tests (already parameterized over both prefixes) as the wire-level\n  behavioural diff.\n- Gates: focused provider tests plus `make test`, `make lint`, `make typecheck` in this worktree.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Every provider the matrix marks Responses-ready (hosted OpenAI, row 1) resolves to\n      `openai-responses:` explicitly; every retained `openai-chat:` path (custom endpoints, rows\n      2-3; other vendors, rows 4-9) is justified by the cited matrix row.\n- [ ] The contract tests are re-run against the migrated paths and the behavioural diff is\n      recorded (structured output, streaming, tool calls, retries, custom base URLs).\n- [ ] A per-provider fallback to `openai-chat:` exists, is documented, emits a deprecation notice,\n      and has a named pre-v1 removal target (`v1.0.0`) recorded via the deprecation registry.\n- [ ] Configuration/migration docs explain the observable wire-semantic changes and how to\n      exercise the fallback.\n- [ ] Focused provider tests plus `make test`, `make lint`, `make typecheck` pass."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787568980502448001,"uuid":"8bc735d3-9e1d-4aae-b1e0-bc8c95956d3f"}